  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "While inspecting the compiler warnings i stumbled over this in DOReaderCache.put(DOReader reader):",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "attrs": {
      "language": "java"
     },
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "String pid = null;\n        try {\n            pid = reader.GetObjectPID();\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n        }\n        Long time = new Long(System.currentTimeMillis());\n        List l = new ArrayList();\n        l.add(reader);\n        l.add(time);",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "codeBlock"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "later this list gets added to a Map m_readers, with the PID being the Key.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "As you can see two different types (String, Long) get added to a List and type and semantics are dependent on the index in the list only. Although Lists are guaranteed to be ordered  i imho consider this an anti-pattern since  it makes lots of things more complex then they need to be.  (e.g. Collections.sort()).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
